NAME
       glxgears - draw three rotating gears, report frame rate

SYNOPSIS
       glxgears [-display displayname] [-info] [-fullscreen] [-geometry WxH]

DESCRIPTION
       glxgears renders the classic animated gears through GLX and prints a
       frames-per-second figure every five seconds.  On LikeOS all rendering
       is performed in software by Mesa's llvmpipe rasterizer; the reported
       rate measures CPU rasterization and XShm presentation, not a GPU.

OPTIONS
       -display displayname
              Connect to the named X display instead of $DISPLAY.

       -info  Print the GL renderer, version and extension strings first.

       -fullscreen
              Run fullscreen rather than in a window.

       -geometry WxH
              Initial window size.

SEE ALSO
       glxinfo(1), eglinfo(1)

